Prefer chosen CPUs for timeshare threads: pcpu=<mask> and rcpu=<mask> (fajita, both default off).

The BCM2837 configuration builds the clutch scheduler without __AMP__, so the SDM845's Kryo 385 Gold cores
(logical 4-7) and Silver cores (0-3) are one undifferentiated pset, and choose_processor() takes the lowest
numbered idle CPU first: a CPU-bound thread usually lands on a Silver core. The pset's perfcontrol preferred
and migration bitmasks, which CLPC sets through the edge scheduler on Apple parts, are already honoured by
choose_processor() on every scheduler; nothing sets them here. pcpu=<mask> seeds them in pset_init (preferred
= mask, migration = the rest), and the clutch thread_avoid_processor() gets the edge scheduler's quantum
expiry check, so a running thread also moves to an idle CPU of the mask. rcpu=<mask> recommends only the CPUs
of the mask instead (a measurement aid). sched_pcpu_tick(), called once a second by package/BootLog.c, applies
rcpu as CPUs come online and fills the two [sched] rows of the UFS log. Touches only osfmk/kern processor.c,
sched_prim.c and sched_clutch.c, which no other patch changes (it applies to pristine xnu-10063.141.1).
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/processor.c b/osfmk/kern/processor.c
index c69d246..2535424 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/processor.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/processor.c
@@ -566,6 +566,8 @@ pset_find(
 /*
  *	Initialize the given processor_set structure.
  */
+extern uint64_t sched_pcpu_mask;   /* fajita: sched_prim.c */
+
 void
 pset_init(
 	processor_set_t         pset,
@@ -613,6 +615,11 @@ pset_init(
 	 */
 	pset->perfcontrol_cpu_preferred_bitmask = 0;
 	pset->perfcontrol_cpu_migration_bitmask = 0;
+	/* fajita: pcpu=<mask> prefers those CPUs and avoids the rest (sched_prim.c, patches/xnu/fajita-pcpu.patch) */
+	if (sched_pcpu_mask != 0) {
+		pset->perfcontrol_cpu_preferred_bitmask = sched_pcpu_mask;
+		pset->perfcontrol_cpu_migration_bitmask = ~sched_pcpu_mask;
+	}
 	pset->cpu_preferred_last_chosen = -1;
 
 	pset->stealable_rt_threads_earliest_deadline = UINT64_MAX;
